// T1 / S12.12: the Symmetric constraint (Shift+Q): "an axis line, then two entities". Compare
// reference/onshape/constraints.md and constraints/constraints-01.png. A vertical construction
// axis, two lines, two circles and two short lines below.
// - Tool first: Shift+Q, then the axis, then the two lines: the right line jumps to the left
//   one's mirror image and both get the "Σ" symmetric glyph. The axis stays picked for the
//   next pair (Onshape pre-selects the axis): the two circles become mirror images too.
// - Selection first: the axis and two points selected, then Constraints ▾ › Symmetric (now
//   enabled in the menu): the points become symmetric and the selection clears.
Scenario(
    start: Some("document"),
    steps: [
        WaitFor("document-shell"),
        Wait(30),
        Click(ui("sketch")),
        WaitFor("sketch-dialog"),
        Wait(3),
